{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_adr_0028_candidacy_is_a_state_somebody_declares", "label": "ADR 0028 Candidacy is a state somebody declares", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/adr/0028-candidacy-is-a-state-somebody-declares.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_adr_0028_candidacy_is_a_state_somebody_declares_candidate_field", "label": "Candidate custom field", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/0028-candidacy-is-a-state-somebody-declares.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Text (Forge cannot declare a checkbox or select); Yes/Y/True case-insensitively; a site with a real checkbox points orgConfig.askField at it."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0028_candidacy_is_a_state_somebody_declares_candidacy_is_a_state", "label": "Candidacy is a state, not a type", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/adr/0028-candidacy-is-a-state-somebody-declares.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A committed, half-built epic is not being weighed; sequencing it would look like advice. A type is permanent, candidacy becomes true and stops being true, so somebody has to say it."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0028_candidacy_is_a_state_somebody_declares_ask_field", "label": "orgConfig.askField", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/0028-candidacy-is-a-state-somebody-declares.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "'app' reads the declared Candidate field; any other value names a site field matched by id then display name \u2014 an instruction, not a guess, unlike findBusinessValueField."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0028_candidacy_is_a_state_somebody_declares_candidate_answer_four_answers", "label": "candidate_answer: None / True / False / str", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/0028-candidacy-is-a-state-somebody-declares.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "None is silence (a band may speak), True yes, False no (beats a band), str an unreadable answer reported with the words written. None-vs-False is load-bearing: the first amendment read 'is not False' and made every epic a candidate."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0028_candidacy_is_a_state_somebody_declares_candidacy_decided_in_resolver", "label": "Candidacy is decided in the resolver, costing a JS mirror", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/adr/0028-candidacy-is-a-state-somebody-declares.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Deciding it in the calculator would send the unreadable answers ('Maybe', 'ask Priya') \u2014 customer free text \u2014 out of the tenant. What crosses is id, sizing method, amount and date; the resolver joins title and basis back by id (a lookup, like reattach)."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0028_candidacy_is_a_state_somebody_declares_ask_payload_guard", "label": "assertAsksCarryNoText / _refuse_ask_text", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/0028-candidacy-is-a-state-somebody-declares.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Asks are built, not projected through the allow-list, so /v1/sequence and /v1/ask accepted a title until this guard."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0028_candidacy_is_a_state_somebody_declares_tshirt_band_declares_candidacy", "label": "A t-shirt band declares candidacy (amendment)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/adr/0028-candidacy-is-a-state-somebody-declares.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Reverses the refusal to infer, for one field only: four screen configuratio